612-As shown in the illustration, the maximum event time tracked by the engine is the
613:*blue dashed line*, and the watermark set as `(max event time - '10 mins')`
614-at the beginning of every trigger is the red line. For example, when the engine observes the data
615:`(12:14, dog)`, it sets the watermark for the next trigger as `12:04`.
616:This watermark lets the engine maintain intermediate state for additional 10 minutes to allow late
617-data to be counted. For example, the data `(12:09, cat)` is out of order and late, and it falls in
618:windows `12:00 - 12:10` and `12:05 - 12:15`. Since, it is still ahead of the watermark `12:04` in
619-the trigger, the engine still maintains the intermediate counts as state and correctly updates the
620:counts of the related windows. However, when the watermark is updated to `12:11`, the intermediate
621-state for window `(12:00 - 12:10)` is cleared, and all subsequent data (e.g. `(12:04, donkey)`)
622-is considered "too late" and therefore ignored. Note that after every trigger,
